+# sae-ethos-pipeline v1.3.1 (PROPOSED, not tagged): fix serving modes for profiles that set determinism flags (2026-11-03)
+
+**Fix.** In v1.3.0 a serving mode's flag replacements were applied only to the lineup's determinism list. Profiles whose
+`serve.extra_args` set the same flags kept their strict values, because the command builder never repeats a flag a
+profile already sets.
+- **Qwen3.5-9B and Qwen3.5-27B** set `--max-num-seqs 1 --no-enable-prefix-caching` in their profiles. Under
+  `throughput` they therefore ran with one sequence in flight. Prefix caching came on only because the mode's
+  `--enable-prefix-caching` came after the profile's `--no-` flag on the command line.
+- Missing Piece's S0-GPU run found this in the server log: `Running: 1 reqs, Waiting: 27 reqs`.
+- From v1.3.1, a non-strict mode rewrites those flags in the profile's args as well. Each flag appears once, with the
+  mode's value.
+
+**Strict mode is unchanged.** Its command is byte-identical to v1.2.0 for all five models (Missing Piece
+`gates/S0/link_check/`).
+
+**Tests.** New: the full command (profile args included) for every model under every mode has each flag once, prefix
+caching on and 32 sequences; the strict command is unchanged. `pytest pipeline/lineup/tests`: 58 pass, 24 skipped.
+
